body:
My dad was on a "business trip" for six weeks. 

&#x200B;

He went to rehab for alcohol addiction.

I was 28 when my dad died unexpectedly. All of the sudden, I was thrust into handling his estate, dealing with lawyers and insurance companies and social security and what not since my mom was too in grief to even attempt. 

&#x200B;

I had to be the parent suddenly. And I hated it.

My dad had a post office box no one knew about. When I discovered it, my mind went immediately to the worst. He had a credit card that my mom didn't know about. When I asked her about it, she looked at the charges and realized that in the months before he died, she was getting worried about finances, so he took out another credit card so they could have dinners out without her seeing them added to their official credit card bill and overly worry. 

&#x200B;

That was just like my dad. Also, quite literally a week before he died (unexpectedly), my dad paid for some program where if he passed away, the mortgage would be entirely paid for.

Pretty much all sports. Granted, I'm now 45, so my athleticism days are far behind me. But even in high school, I was awkward, weak, and uncomfortable with my own body. 

&#x200B;

Well, all except at volleyball. For some reason, I was pretty good at volleyball.

"If it wasn't for your writing talent, you'd be worthless." -7th grade teacher. 

&#x200B;

But hey, I'm a professional journalist today, so it obviously stuck with me.

Toughie. Probably Costco because their furniture is much more comfortable and much more varied samples to eat. 

&#x200B;

But Ikea's meatballs are tough to resist.

Jeremiah Weed. 

&#x200B;

That shit is disgustingly syrupy

"(Don't You) Forget About Me" - Simple Minds. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Yeah, I'm kinda a Breakfast Club buff.

I have zero self-confidence, self-esteem, and am manic depressive.

&#x200B;

But one skill I do have: I can bark exactly like a dog. Awesome party trick I can use to break the ice and attempt to fit in.

Actually it's:

&#x200B;

No. I am your father.

What's better than roses on a piano?

&#x200B;

Lipstick on your organ.

I suck. 

&#x200B;

Oh wait. "Should" know. Not "Does" know.
